Subject: [M150] Post task for PrepareToLeaveBackForwardCache callback

Original change's description:
> Post task for PrepareToLeaveBackForwardCache callback
>
> When a FrameTree shuts down, FrameTree::Shutdown() calls
> ClearRFHsPendingShutdown() on each FrameTreeNode before resetting
> ongoing NavigationRequests.
>
> Destroying a pending-delete RenderFrameHostImpl can destroy its
> RenderViewHostImpl. If that RenderViewHostImpl had an unanswered
> SetPageLifecycleState Mojo message from
> RenderViewHostImpl::PrepareToLeaveBackForwardCache(), destroying the
> RenderViewHostImpl invokes the default Mojo response callback via
> mojo::WrapCallbackWithDefaultInvokeIfNotRun(). When an in-flight
> BackForwardCache restore NavigationRequest is waiting on that
> callback in BackForwardCacheImpl::WillCommitNavigationToCachedEntry(),
> the callback synchronously commits the restore during
> FrameTree::Shutdown(), causing
> RenderFrameHostManager::UnloadOldFrame() to insert into
> pending_delete_hosts_ while std::set::clear() is iterating over it.
>
> Fix this by:
> 1. Wrapping the callback in
>    RenderViewHostImpl::PrepareToLeaveBackForwardCache() with
>    base::BindPostTaskToCurrentDefault() so that destroying a
>    RenderViewHostImpl (e.g. during shutdown or on an unload timeout)
>    never synchronously triggers a BackForwardCache restore commit in
>    the middle of ~RenderFrameHostImpl() / ~RenderViewHostImpl().
> 2. Swapping pending_delete_hosts_ into a local set in
>    RenderFrameHostManager::ClearRFHsPendingShutdown() before clearing
>    it, and asserting that pending_delete_hosts_ remains empty
>    afterward.
>
